<title>USA: American Radio sells 2 Omaha stations.</title>
<headline>American Radio sells 2 Omaha stations.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Radio Systems Corp said on Friday after the market closed that it has reached an agreement to sell radio stations KGOR-FM and KFAB-AM in Omaha, Nebraska to Triathlon Broadcasting Co for $39 million.</p>
<p>The company said it expects that the sale will be finalized during the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>A company spokesman was not available to say whether American Radio will record a gain or a loss on the sale.</p>
</text>
